{#
  Fine print on a record, minus the site-wide rights line.

  "©1998 SCVTV/SCVHistory.com & SANTA CLARITA VALLEY HISTORICAL SOCIETY ·
  RIGHTS RESERVED." is true of every page on the site, so printing it under
  every record said the same thing 51 times and read as part of the article.
  It is in the footer now, once, with the year derived.

  The value stays in finePrint on the record because it is provenance and the
  JSON-LD and the Dublin Core rights tag both read it. Only the printing stops.

  What does not stop is everything else in that field. Six records carry
  something that is not the site-wide line and each of them still prints:

    ©A.B. Perkins/Santa Clarita Valley Historical Society Collection
    ©Historical Society of Southern California | Presentation ©2013 SCVHistory.com
    Obituary courtesy of Stan Walker.
    and three scan credit lines that belong in creditRaw and have not moved yet

  The first two are rights held by somebody else, which the footer's line does
  not cover and must not be taken to cover.

  Usage: {% include "_partials/record/fine-print" with { value: F.finePrint } only %}
#}
{%- set v = value|default('')|trim -%}
{%- set flat = v|replace({'\n': ' '})|trim -%}
{#- The standard line in all the spellings the corpus holds: with and without
    SCVTV, with and without SCVHistory.com, a year or two years or none, a
    middle dot or a full stop, "Rights reserved" or "All rights reserved". -#}
{%- set STANDARD = '~^\\s*\\x{00a9}\\s*[\\d/,\\s]*\\s*(SCVTV\\s*/\\s*)?(SCVHistory\\.com\\s*&\\s*)?SANTA CLARITA VALLEY HISTORICAL SOCIETY\\s*[\\x{00b7}\\x{2022}|.,]?\\s*(ALL )?RIGHTS RESERVED\\.?\\s*$~iu' -%}
{%- if v != '' and not (flat matches STANDARD) -%}
  <p class="rec-fine">{{ v }}</p>
{%- endif -%}
